<para><verbatim>embed:rst
The BlockShuffle class provides :ref:`collective &lt;collective-primitives&gt;`
methods for shuffling data partitioned across a CUDA thread block.

Overview
++++++++++++++++

It is commonplace for blocks of threads to rearrange data items between threads.
The BlockShuffle abstraction allows threads to efficiently shift items either
(a) up to their successor or
(b) down to their predecessor</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The data type to be exchanged.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>BLOCK_DIM_X</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The thread block length in threads along the X dimension</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>BLOCK_DIM_Y</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><bold>[optional]</bold> The thread block length in threads along the Y dimension (default: 1)</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>BLOCK_DIM_Z</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><bold>[optional]</bold> The thread block length in threads along the Z dimension (default: 1) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
